"Hand casting weaves authority through imaginary symbols traced by finger patterns in the air."
"Spells carry ingredients, tools and chants through the maze of reality to a new destination."
"Chants need more octaves than a human voice, often one spell said aloud and another in the head."
"A caster must mean what they say."
"Spells draw only on free authority, not authority bound to skills or traits."
"Perception covers minor casting mistakes; talented wizards push spells where they shouldn't go."
"Child spells include musical notes, lighting promise sticks, puffs of air and hand sanitizing."
"Casting with intention feels like becoming more, and may be addictive for wizards."
